.TH MD_NEW_IQ 3 "2026-10-16" "libmorsedec 0.2.0" "Library Functions Manual"
.SH NAME
md_new_iq \- create a streaming complex I/Q decoder
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <morsedec.h>

morsedec_decoder_t * md_new_iq(const struct morsedec_config
    *config);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Create a streaming complex I/Q decoder.
.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I config
Configuration to copy, or NULL for 48 kHz, -1200..1200 Hz and otherwise audio
defaults.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns an owned decoder handle on success, or NULL and sets errno on failure.
.SH ERRORS
.TP
.B EINVAL
Invalid configuration, signed band or geometry.
.TP
.B ENOMEM
Storage allocation or FFT planning failed.
.SH REMARKS
Accepts I+jQ input: I=cos(2*pi*f*t), Q=sin(2*pi*f*t) produces a positive f Hz
offset. sample_rate counts complex pairs per second. Retained band edges may
be negative and must describe a nonempty subband of [-sample_rate/2,
sample_rate/2); the upper edge is exclusive. With an explicit config, all
fields are used as supplied: md_config_init() does not choose symmetric I/Q
defaults.
.PP
Channel frequencies and geometry are signed Hz offsets from the stream IF
center at 0 Hz. No RF center frequency is added. There is no built-in
frequency translation, resampling, DC-offset removal or I/Q-imbalance
correction. I and Q must retain their order; swapping them reverses frequency
orientation. Pass interleaved pairs to md_process_iq() or md_process_iq_s16().
Mono processing calls are invalid for this handle. External power frames are
also supported on the signed ascending grid. Ownership, allocation and
lifetime match md_new().
.SH THREAD SAFETY
Serialize this call with all FFTW planner and plan-destruction operations in
the application, including operations for other handles.
.SH VERSION
This md_ entry point is available since libmorsedec 0.2.0 (shared-library ABI
1).
